<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - SA Eagle H1 shr, div jumps.</title>
<headline>TABLE - SA Eagle H1 shr, div jumps.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		579.0	 vs 312.8</p>
<p>    - post-exceps	   1,014.0     vs 425.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 125.0	 vs 100.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   123.50	vs 51.77</p>
<p>    Pre-tax operating     159.61	vs 70.39</p>
<p>    Tax			 36.00	 vs 18.60</p>
<p>    Investment expense    1.34	  vs 1.48</p>
<p>    Investment income     85.22	 vs 56.07</p>
<p>    Underwriting profit   19.20	 vs 2.02</p>
<p>    Gross writtem premium 823.10	vs 794.53</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     56.52	 vs 13.78</p>
<p>Div payable Sept 12</p>
<p>on register Aug 15</p>
<p>Full name: South African Eagle Insurance Co Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said the exceptional item related to a net realised surplus on the disposal of investments.</p>
<p>They said that the results at the half year were not necessarily indicative of full year results, but gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
